e stated caller contract ('must not read latest findings while false') would then permanently suppress a valid current sidecar written by a prior non-readonly run"],"finding":"The receipt mechanism conflates a read-only run's by-design no-emit with a failed emit: a readonly review_plan_start records sidecar_emitted=false with no receipt, which the plan maps to reason 'sidecar-not-emitted' and findings.readable=false permanently, hiding a legitimately-current prior-run sidecar the caller should be allowed to read.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f71dae627b07a13d8","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan step 4 / Disposition paragraph ('sidecar-not-emitted is a new record with sidecar_emitted=false and no receipt'); _mcp_llm._review_plan_body emit_sidecar=not readonly","norm_id":"nb2cbd427daddbfa2","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A caller uses review_plan_start (the recommended timeout-proof path) in a deployment where the async start runs read-only, polls gate_status, sees terminal + findings.readable=false reason=sidecar-not-emitted, and never reads the current findings a prior real review left"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Carry a distinct disposition (e.g. reason='review-result-emit-skipped-readonly') when the terminal record was produced with emit_sidecar=false because the run was read-only, and state explicitly whether callers may read the durable/latest findings in that state rather than folding it into the general sidecar-not-emitted 'do not read' contract.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Assign an explicit findings.reason value for the reused-receipt readable case (either reuse current-review-result-sidecar and state so, or add a distinct reason) and pin it in Acceptance Criteria bullet 5.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Disposition: 'current-review-result-sidecar is readable' — the only readable reason named","AC-5 asserts readable=true but omits the reason string, unlike sibling ACs which each pin reason= (e.g. reason=\"current-review-result-sidecar\", reason=\"sidecar-not-emitted\")","reuse.py verdict_reuse/idempotent_reuse set sidecar_emitted=False and point at a PRIOR run's sidecar, so labeling it 'current' is semantically ambiguous"],"finding":"The reused-receipt readable case (sidecar_emitted=false carrying a reused sidecar_reviewed_at) has no assigned findings.reason value: AC-5 asserts readable=true 'for that exact sidecar' but names no reason, and the Disposition lists only current-review-result-sidecar as the readable reason while describing that reason as the freshly-emitted current sidecar.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f33b578ffe8d73555","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan step 4 / step 7; Disposition paragraph; Acceptance Criteria bullet 5 ('terminal sidecar_emitted=false with a reused sidecar_reviewed_at reports findings.readable=true')","norm_id":"n29e41670443e7e43","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A BLOCK verdict_reuse run: caller polls, gets readable=true, but the reason string is undefined — an agent branching on reason cannot classify it","A caller allow-listing reason values to gate a read rejects the reused case because its reason is unspecified"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Co-locate an explicit discriminator/precedence rule with the reason list stating how gate_runs.py separates sidecar-not-emitted (sidecar_emitted key present and false, no receipt) from review-result-generation-unknown (no receipt fields at all, legacy).","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Both reasons are described with the phrase 'no receipt'/'no receipt fields', so the differentiator is implicit (the presence-but-false sidecar_emitted key)","gate_runs.py terminal records today carry neither sidecar_emitted nor sidecar_reviewed_at, so legacy records lack the key entirely while step 5 adds it going forward — the reader must branch on key presence, which the plan never states as the rule","No processing-protocol/precedence statement co-locates 'if sidecar_emitted key absent → generation-unknown; if present and false without receipt → sidecar-not-emitted' with the enum"],"finding":"The decision rule distinguishing the NEW sidecar-not-emitted record from the LEGACY review-result-generation-unknown record is under-specified: both are described as having 'no receipt', and the discriminator (presence of a sidecar_emitted=false key vs total absence of receipt fields) plus its precedence is not co-located with the reason vocabulary that needs it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4282844054a1562b","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Disposition paragraph ('sidecar-not-emitted is a new record with sidecar_emitted=false and no receipt; review-result-generation-unknown is a legacy terminal record with no receipt fields'); Fix plan step 6/7","norm_id":"n38847ae8704b6aa5","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A pre-fix terminal index entry (no sidecar_emitted key) polled after upgrade","A new terminal BLOCK where sidecar.emit returned false (sidecar_emitted=false, no receipt) polled and must NOT be misread as legacy"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State the rule as an ordered branch: (1) exact sidecar_reviewed_at present → readable check; (2) sidecar_emitted==false present → sidecar-not-emitted; (3) neither key present → review-result-generation-unknown.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","n