licitly names the stale/crashed-leader case, so it is unclear whether `run-stale-running` is expected to satisfy the `run-<status>` pattern or is a separate untested reason."],"finding":"The Disposition names a `run-stale-running` reason (crashed-leader unavailable state), but no acceptance criterion covers it; the non-terminal AC only asserts `reason=\"run-<status>\"` for running/attaching, leaving `run-stale-running` unproven.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc9f4fcf2f72b1811","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan / Disposition paragraph; Acceptance Criteria (non-terminal AC)","norm_id":"ne21ce39b90a8f088","priority":0.165,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A crashed leader leaves a run in the stale state and a caller polls gate_status expecting a defined reason."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the caller-facing disposition (retryable vs fatal) for a stamped-but-permanently-unreadable exact-prefix receipt, distinguishing permanent corruption/absence (fatal) from a sidecar still being written (retryable) under `review-result-sidecar-missing`.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'`review-result-sidecar-missing` covers absent, unreadable, corrupt, or unsupported exact-prefix files; callers may keep polling only under their normal bounded wait policy and must not read latest findings while false.'","Root-cause section lists 'permanent sidecar failure' as one of the confusable states the fix is meant to disambiguate, yet the terminal permanent-failure case (emit succeeded, receipt stamped, file later corrupt) shares the retryable `review-result-sidecar-missing` disposition."],"finding":"The plan collapses permanent, unrecoverable sidecar unreadability (a receipt was stamped — sidecar_emitted=true, sidecar_reviewed_at set — but the exact-prefix file is permanently missing/corrupt) into the same `review-result-sidecar-missing` reason as a sidecar still being written, and prescribes only 'keep polling under bounded wait'. There is no distinct terminal/fatal disposition for a stamped-but-permanently-unreadable receipt, so a caller cannot distinguish a transient (retryable) not-yet-written state from a permanent (fatal) failure and will poll until timeout on a case that will never resolve.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f11f484da8ed74fce","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan step 7 and Disposition paragraph: 'review-result-sidecar-missing covers absent, unreadable, corrupt, or unsupported exact-prefix files; callers may keep polling only under their normal bounded wait policy'","norm_id":"nab8460da0ec9d2e0","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A run stamps sidecar_reviewed_at (emit returned true) but the exact-prefix file is written corrupt or subsequently truncated: gate_status reports terminal + readable=false + review-result-sidecar-missing indefinitely; the caller keeps polling (retryable) until its bounded wait expires though the state is fatal and will never become readable."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify how latest_review_result() exposes the exact filename timestamp (separate return value/tuple vs. an in-payload key) and confirm reuse.py can obtain it without disturbing the existing payload-by-key consumers (drift_floor/resign/remediation_mode/retry/cited_anchor).","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.666,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'annotate latest_review_result() with the exact filename timestamp of the payload it returns'","Plan step 4: reuse paths 'set sidecar_reviewed_at from the reused sidecar's filename timestamp'","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py:148 latest_review_result returns only the deserialized `data` payload (schema/findings/coverage), NOT the filename","reuse.py:218/143 and drift_floor.py, resign.py, remediation_mode.py, retry.py, cited_anchor.py all read the returned payload by key"],"finding":"The sidecar.py scope line ('annotate latest_review_result() with the exact filename timestamp of the payload it returns') and Fix-plan step 4 (reuse paths set sidecar_reviewed_at 'from the reused sidecar's filename timestamp') do not specify HOW latest_review_result() exposes that timestamp — whether it mutates a new key into the returned data payload dict or changes the return type. latest_review_result() currently returns only the deserialized data payload, which multiple plan_review consumers destructure by key (verdict_reuse/idempotent_reuse read prior.get('findings')/('ticket_type')/('material_fingerprint'); drift_floor, resign, remediation_mode, retry, cited_anchor also read it). If the annotation mutates the returned dict, those consumers see an extra key; if it changes the signature, reuse.py's call sites must unpack it. The plan leaves this unspecified even though step 4 depends on reuse.py obtaining the timestamp.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb02ffee2733b89cb","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope/file impact: src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py line; Fix plan step 4","norm_id":"n1b5018a42f7ca64d","priority":0.134,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["verdict_reuse needs the filename timestamp to set sidecar_reviewed_at but latest_review_result() does not currently return it","An in-payload annotation key could leak into payloads compared/replayed by reuse or equality-checked in tests"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"n